# termiHub first-party plugin publisher key -- the bundled trust anchor (#3980).
#
# TERMIHUB-FIRST-PARTY-PLUGIN-KEY-PLACEHOLDER
#
# This file is a PLACEHOLDER: no real first-party publisher key has been generated
# yet. While it contains no PUBLIC KEY block, the desktop compiles in NO bundled
# publisher: every trusted plugin publisher is a trust-on-first-use (TOFU) pin in
# <app-data>/plugins/trust-store.json, exactly as before (#2796). Packaging CI
# leaves first-party plugins unsigned. This key is SEPARATE from the agent update
# signing key and from the plugin-index signing key.
#
# The maintainer replaces this file by running (once):
#
#   ./scripts/internal/setup-plugin-publisher-key.sh
#
# which generates an ed25519 keypair, stores the private key ONLY as the
# FIRST_PARTY_PLUGIN_SIGNING_KEY GitHub Actions secret (used by the "Plugin
# Packaging" workflow to sign first-party plugin packages), and rewrites this file
# with the public key in PEM (SubjectPublicKeyInfo) form. From then on that key is
# compiled into every desktop as an immutable `bundled` publisher: first-party
# plugins verify without any user pin, and no trust-store.json edit can remove or
# replace it. See docs/contributing.md -> "First-party plugin publisher key".
